== MEANING
Only the standard library reads a tree's child field generically
(std::tree::walk). A program that walks a value whose type is no tree
struct sees this as the TYPE error of its call to std::tree::walk ("call
to std::tree::walk with root : int ... is invalid"), whose explanation is
this one.

== WHAT TO DO
Walk a value of a tree struct type (`tree struct NAME:`); to traverse
another recursive structure, write the traversal as a function over its
fields.
